WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.760
A bean plant has a whole life, and it is a circle.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.520
A seed sprouts, grows leaves and flowers, and makes pods with new seeds.

3
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.500
Then the plant dies, and the new seeds can start the circle again.

4
00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:20.463
You need bush bean seeds labelled untreated, potting mix, and two or three pots with

5
00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:21.463
drainage holes.

6
00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:25.923
Fill each pot with potting mix to about two centimetres below the rim.

7
00:00:26.743 --> 00:00:29.303
Push two or three seeds about three centimetres deep.

8
00:00:30.103 --> 00:00:31.743
Water until it drips out the bottom.

9
00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:34.223
Set the pot in the sunniest window.

10
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:36.557
Visit once a week.

11
00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:41.577
In warm weather, a hooked stem usually pushes up in five to fourteen days.

12
00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:45.957
Flowers usually open about four to seven weeks after planting.

13
00:00:47.017 --> 00:00:49.637
Flowers come first, then pods that hold new seeds.

14
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.720
Do not eat raw bean pods or seeds.

15
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.680
Keep loose seeds away from children under four.
